---
/**
 * Cinematic home, preserved from the production build.
 *
 * Cloudflare Pages deployment 6b21b14c (preview 6b21b14c.wenu-frontend.pages.dev,
 * live at wenumapuonline.com) serves a film landing — Pelicula, MenuCielo,
 * OraculoDeck, AlmanaqueLuna, and the rest — that is not in any git branch.
 * Searching history for Pelicula.astro, data-peli, and "Wënü Mapü — the film"
 * found nothing. Rebuilding the previous index.astro (HeroCarousel and the
 * older sections, including commit "33 puertas a los mundos") would replace it.
 *
 * src/cine/home.html is that deployment's document, with its CSS/JS vendored
 * under public/_astro/ (the hashes the HTML already references). Shop, PDP,
 * cart, and the other routes still build from source and from WooCommerce.
 *
 * Fidelity: the markup, scoped CSS, and film runtime are the production bytes.
 * The only landing changes are load-order:
 *   1. The opening plane paints immediately. Production CSS clips the first
 *      frame to circle(0%) and hides every plane until Pelicula.js runs, so
 *      the viewport stays obsidian — and at rest the clip stays closed until
 *      you scroll. A poster rule shows /img/hero/hero-cosmos-eclipse.webp at
 *      once. The scroll film still crossfades the later planes.
 *   2. The film stylesheets and Pelicula's module (Lenis + the WebGL film)
 *      load after that still can paint. Later film images are lazy. There is
 *      no <video> file; the "film" is that scripted sequence.
 *
 * Frozen: names and prices inside the home film are from the capture. The
 * catalogue at /shop and /p/[slug] is still read from WooCommerce at build time.
 */
import html from '../cine/home.html?raw';
---
<Fragment set:html={html} />
